description:Extend the Python conformance harness as an independent consumer of the protocol 1.0.0-rc.6 candidate suite at immutable reviewed curator-spec commit 432eb2ee1fe2d6b271e37269f867c8851c325539, matching schema-v6, build-driver, portable execution-policy, identity, cache, context, and expanded manager-lifecycle vectors without advancing a released-suite pin.
scope:Own tests/test_protocol_conformance.py plus focused vector adapters and fixtures that do not duplicate product logic. Consume the exact reviewed rc.6 candidate suite at immutable merged curator-spec commit 432eb2ee1fe2d6b271e37269f867c8851c325539 through the caller-supplied CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT, whose manifest.json must hash to sha256:12e58b82579645ba1ccafba49d3e2dd3216005ddf37ae63c68a9fafd46773071 and whose release/1.0.0-rc.6.json records the same required_manifest_sha256; do not edit the committed curator-spec checkout ref in this task. Read every in-scope schema-v6, go-v1, policy, claim-qualification, expected build-driver, and manager-lifecycle artifact from that root; never hard-code a vector input the way Curator internal/godriver/controls_test.go does. Cover generated schema cases for both manifest names, agent-skill-v6 and csk-skill-v6, receipt build-receipt-v1, marker install-marker-v2, conformance-claim-v3, vectors/build-drivers.json, vectors/go-host-execution-policy.json, vectors/conformance-claim-v3-qualification.json, the 11-file expected/build-driver/ tree, and vectors/manager-lifecycle.json. build-receipt-v2, install-marker-v3, schema v7 and the external-repository and registry surfaces belong to the go-repository-v1 line and are out of scope here. The official manager suite pin remains on the previous released protocol until TASK-260720-25d05o qualifies the release and TASK-260720-1utsx8 audits the promotion. Do not import or copy Curator implementation code and do not fabricate release or conformance claims. Accepted immutable-root prerequisites: TASK-260720-3ag6pi and BUG-260731-2rhy74 are independently accepted done. curator-spec PR #15 merged at GitHub-verified commit 432eb2ee1fe2d6b271e37269f867c8851c325539 with 8/8 Ubuntu/macOS/Windows checks green and publishes the required manifest digest plus expanded 32-case manager lifecycle. Treat this as candidate evidence only: do not create a tag, GitHub Release, released-suite pin, or conformance claim in this task.
ac:The Python implementation passes the shared reviewed rc.6 candidate positive vectors for schema 6, build-root context exclusion, build-source and toolchain bytes, CCJ-1 input and key, canonical receipt and marker, fixed environment and all five Go argv forms, hit and dry-run plans, ordering, commit, rollback, recovery, status, repair, and GC, including all 8 build-drivers.json positive_cases and the byte-exact 11 artifacts under expected/build-driver/ whose cache-key.txt is sha256:529370122ae11e2e961d5265b1a020e046bcd43165b2eb96b05e73a51187ac9b and receipt-sha256.txt is sha256:919fbbad8e6ce95532219fd952c2309d0d7026f85209650508fd6834af4020cd. Named negative coverage includes every minimum cluster from the accepted rc.5 contract: all 77 build-drivers.json rejection_cases, the 10 build_source_cases and 12 toolchain_cases, and from go-host-execution-policy.json the 18 mandatory_controls, the 14 identity_and_protocol_cases, the 8 package_influence_cases, the 11 capability_evidence_cases, the 6 deferred_capability_rejection_guards, and the three failure_boundary outcomes. Execution-policy identity coverage asserts aliases false and three distinct non-alias keys: portable manager-worker-v1 valid, legacy_rc4_without_execution_policy sha256:3fcd714a40e8918eb67dbd35d435875dcce6c9047da811a1fa26626e5e57be48 invalid, and reserved_hardened sha256:13736230d33ce59de7f7323dcd4cffd510655ad8dabd5ee9e8b6cb182ec70037 invalid. Native-control inventory coverage asserts rc5-native-control-inventory-v1 is exhaustive over exactly macos and windows with exactly five controls and the declared per-platform availability and mechanism or reason. Claim coverage asserts claim-version separation across conformance-claim-v1, v2 and v3; the conformance-claim-v3 schema fixtures remain pinned to protocol_version 1.0.0-rc.5 and require build_drivers, while conformance-claim-v3-qualification.json identifies candidate protocol_version 1.0.0-rc.6 and its rules hold: schema-valid-is-not-qualified, driver-platform-subset, no-generic-driver over exactly go-repository-v1 and go-v1, no-unevidenced-platform, linux excluded until TASK-260728-1skseh, and macos and windows pending-downstream-native-evidence. No conformance claim is emitted by this task. Legacy rc.3 vectors remain green. Tests against the exact caller-supplied candidate suite at commit 432eb2ee1fe2d6b271e37269f867c8851c325539 and manifest sha256:12e58b82579645ba1ccafba49d3e2dd3216005ddf37ae63c68a9fafd46773071 and strict mypy pass, the candidate revision and full manifest digest are recorded as non-release evidence, and no committed curator-spec pin or release claim changes.
